Implement `isPortrait()`: `return this.ch > this.cw && this.cw < 900;` (phone/tablet portrait). Maybe use matchMedia but dimensions suffice. For tablet portrait 768x1024, width<900 → rotate overlay. Should tablets in portrait also be asked to rotate? Yes, game needs landscape. Good. For desktop narrow window 500x800, it would show overlay; acceptable.

- `showOnly(el)`: include dom.rotate.
- `showRotate()`: if state playing, state='rotate'; hide hint; showOnly(rotate); showHUD(false). If state is win/lose, don't. Only call from startLevel/resize.
- `resumeFromRotate()`: if state !== 'rotate' return; state='playing'; showOnly(null); showHUD(true); last=now; if level 1 and usedPigs 0 maybe toast. Hide ability hint.
- `startLevel`: after setup/showHUD, if `this.isPortrait() && !this.allowPortrait` → `this.showRotate(); return;` but showOnly(null) and showHUD(true) happen before. Fine. Also don't show level tip toast while rotate; the setTimeout checks state==='playing', so it won't show. Good.
- `resize`: after updating view, if state==='rotate' && !isPortrait → resumeFromRotate. If state==='playing' && isPortrait && !allowPortrait → showRotate. But resizing while playing on desktop to a narrow window would pause and show overlay. Fine. Also if state==='paused' and portrait? no.
- On title portrait, don't show overlay.
- On levels portrait, grid works.
- On "Play Anyway", `this.allowPortrait=true; this.resumeFromRotate();` (state rotate). Also hide rotate hint? The chip still shows; keep.
- If user starts a level in portrait, clicks Play Anyway, then goes levels and starts another level, allowPortrait stays true (session). Good.
- If user rotates to landscape while rotate screen, resume automatically.
- If user rotates back to portrait while playing and allowPortrait false → show rotate. If allowPortrait true, play tiny.
- Need to update state when showRotate from playing; physics stops. When resume, continue.

